# The secrets the realm references and this repository never holds: the
# launch Identity Sources' client ids and secrets. Copy this file to
# `.env.local`, which git ignores, and fill in what you were given;
# compose.yaml hands it to the Broker. Uncomment only the names you have a
# value for. Left out, a name imports as `not-configured`, and the source
# refuses a Person on its own page. Left empty, it is set: the source gets an
# empty client id and the Broker fails before sending anyone there.
#
# The redirect URI each one is registered with is
# `${BROKER_ISSUER}/broker/google/endpoint` and
# `${BROKER_ISSUER}/broker/github/endpoint`. `broker/README.md` says why.

# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
# GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
